This product runs, without modification, software developed by the
Stanford Neuromuscular Biomechanics Laboratory (OpenCap):
  - opencap-core       https://github.com/stanfordnmbl/opencap-core       (Apache License 2.0)
  - opencap-processing https://github.com/stanfordnmbl/opencap-processing (Apache License 2.0)
The Docker images built by docker-compose.yml clone those repositories at the
pinned commits listed in worker_core/Dockerfile and worker_kinetics/Dockerfile.

Uhlrich SD, Falisse A, Kidziński Ł, et al. OpenCap: Human movement dynamics
from smartphone videos. PLoS Comput Biol. 2023;19(10):e1011462.
doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1011462

Dashboard 3D viewer uses three.js r160 (MIT, vendored under dashboard/vendor/three).
Bone meshes are not stored in this repository; the server image downloads them at
build time from the OpenSim models repository:
  https://github.com/opensim-org/opensim-models/tree/master/Geometry

Files derived from opencap-core (Apache License 2.0), modified by PhysioCap contributors in 2026:
  - mmpose_cpu/loop_mmpose_cpu.py — based on opencap-core mmpose/loop_mmpose.py at commit
    e5d29f12e725a2e14e6e4e85617834685f738753. Changes: no GPU check at start; compute device
    taken from PHYSIOCAP_POSE_DEVICE (default cpu); smaller batch and all CPU threads on CPU;
    per-step timing in the log. Same models, threshold and input/output files.
  - mmpose_cpu/benchmark_pose.py — new timing script that calls opencap-core's
    detection_inference and pose_inference on a clip of OpenCap's public test video
    (downloaded at run time from stanfordnmbl/opencap-test-data; not redistributed here).
  - worker_core/keypoint_mode.py — new code for the optional "keypoints" kinematics method. At run
    time it writes an IK setup file that is opencap-core's opensimPipeline/IK/Setup_IK_mmpose.xml
    with added IKCoordinateTask entries (weak regularization toward 0 deg), and it uses
    opencap-core's Setup_scaling_LaiUhlrich2022_mmpose.xml and LaiUhlrich2022_markers_mmpose.xml
    unchanged. opencap-core itself is not modified.

Third-party software inside the Docker images (built from upstream sources at install time,
not stored in this repository). Anyone who redistributes the built images must follow
these licenses as well:
  - CasADi (kinetics image, via opencap-processing): GNU LGPL v3
  - FFmpeg in the core image (Ubuntu package 3.4.11): built with --enable-gpl and libx264,
    so the binary is under the GNU GPL. The server image installs Debian's ffmpeg package;
    check its build configuration ("ffmpeg -version") before redistributing that image too.
  - OpenSim 4.5 (conda): Apache-2.0; OpenSimAD libraries: Apache-2.0
  - mmpose / mmdetection (pose image): Apache-2.0
